-- title:
--   Maximal orders in a definite quaternion algebra over ℚ are adelically conjugate
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be rationals and let $p$ be a prime, and suppose the predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L87) holds for $a$, $b$ and $p$: that is, $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, the $v$-adic algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has every nonzero element a unit precisely when $p$ lies in the prime ideal attached to $v$. Let $\Lambda_0$ and $\Lambda$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, each a maximal order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L63): each is an order, i.e. contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$, and each is equal to any order containing it. The conclusion is that there exists a unit $y$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ being used, such that [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $\Lambda_0\,y=\Lambda$; by definition the left-hand side is the set of quaternions in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image in the adelic algebra lies in $y\,\widehat{\Lambda_0}\,y^{-1}$, where $\widehat{\Lambda_0}$ is the additive subgroup generated by the products $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_0$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele that is integral at every place.
--
--   This is the statement that in a definite quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ ramified at exactly one prime any two maximal orders are conjugate by a finite idele, the global consequence of local conjugacy of maximal orders together with the fact that a lattice is determined by its localisations. It is used to show that every maximal order arises, up to the relevant identification, as the endomorphism ring of a supersingular elliptic curve, in [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_supersingular_rationalEndSubring_range_eq_of_isMaximalOrder`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_supersingular_rationalEndSubring_range_eq_of_isMaximalOrder).
